# Goal: Implement Module 4 Workflow Configuration

Implement a persistent, configurable, and high-fidelity Workflow Configuration feature matching the Stitch design (Screen ID `b59da977436d4d05a48d53bc4db6ddfd`). This enables administrators to define multi-level approval chains with distinct SLA rules, conditions, and automated escalation parameters, satisfying Sprints 5 & 6 requirements of the Workflow Management Module.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Tab Switcher on Approvals Page**: For Admin users, we will render a tab selector at the top of the **Team Approvals** page allowing toggling between the **Approvals Queue** and the **Workflow Configuration** screen.
> - **Seed Rules**: We will seed a default "Standard Approval Workflow" with three predefined levels (Direct Manager up to $5,000, Finance/Dept Head for Travel/Hardware or values > $5,000, and Executive Approval for values > $50,000) on backend start.
> - **Multi-Level Approval Logic**: The backend approval service will be upgraded to check for matching workflow rules, progressing expenses level-by-level rather than immediately marking them as fully approved.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Components

---

#### [NEW] [workflow-rule.schema.ts](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/backend/src/modules/workflow/schemas/workflow-rule.schema.ts)
- Create schema for `WorkflowRule` storing:
  - `name`: String
  - `isActive`: Boolean
  - `levels`: Array of workflow levels, each with `level` (Number), `name` (String), `description` (String), `limit` (Number), `slaHours` (Number), `autoEscalate` (Boolean), and `condition` (String).

#### [MODIFY] [workflow.module.ts](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/backend/src/modules/workflow/workflow.module.ts)
